    "q-106075": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106075",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find a point that satisfies the mean value theorem for $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y$ on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ where the position vectors of $A$ and $B$ are $a=⟨0,1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩,$ respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The mean value theorem states that if $f(x,y)$ is differentiable at each point on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ then there exists a point $C\\in \\overset{―}{AB}$ with position vector $c$ such that\n\n$$\nf(b)-f(a)=∇f(c)·(b-a).\n$$\n\nNotice that the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y$ is differentiable at each point on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ So, we can apply the mean value theorem.\n\nSubstituting $a=⟨0,1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩$ into the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,3)-f(0,1) & =∇f(c)\\cdot (⟨1,3⟩-⟨0,1⟩) \\\\ ({1}^{2}+3)-({0}^{2}+1) & =∇f(c)\\cdot ⟨1,2⟩ \\\\ 3 & =∇f(c)\\cdot ⟨1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $∇f$ and evaluating at $c=⟨{c}_{1},{c}_{2}⟩,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2x,1⟩, \\\\ ∇f(c) & =⟨2{c}_{1},1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =∇f⟨c⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2⟩ \\\\ 3 & =⟨2{c}_{1},1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2⟩ \\\\ 3 & =2{c}_{1}+2 \\\\ 1 & =2{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $C$ lies on $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ So, let's first find the equation of the line.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y-{y}_{a}}{{y}_{b}-{y}_{a}} & =\\frac{x-{x}_{a}}{{x}_{b}-{x}_{a}} \\\\ \\frac{y-1}{3-1} & =\\frac{x-0}{1-0} \\\\ \\frac{y-1}{2} & =x \\\\ y & =2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $c=⟨{c}_{1},{c}_{2}⟩$ satisfies the equation of the line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} & =2{c}_{1}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking into account that ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2},$ we obtain that ${c}_{2}=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+1=2.$ So, the point $C$ that satisfies the mean value theorem is $(\\frac{1}{2},2).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-106075-a",
